      },
      {
         "id": "SECTION_introduction",
         "text": [
            {
               "text": "### Introduction\n\nIn the two previous texts about multiplication, we learned that people created a new operation to make repeated addition easier. This leads us to the following reflection",
               "source": null,
               "date_time": null,
               "isTable": false,
               "imgdesc": "",
               "format": "markdown",
               "PostMention": ":"
            },
            {
               "text": "<p><center><div class=\"first_steps_reflection_parent\"><div class=\"first_steps_reflection question_mark\"><i class=\"fa-solid fa-brain\"></i></div><div class=\"first_steps_reflection\"><b>Reflection 1: Reaching Conclusions</b><br /><br />In the <i>General History</i> section (<htcite0>), we observed that various peoples developed cultures and civilizations independently.<br /><br />Did they also arrive at the same mathematical conclusions?</div></div></center></p>",
               "source": [
                  {
                     "type": 1,
                     "uuid": "867968ea-62d6-4a8a-b3a0-8b82c76d86bf",
                     "text": "History Tracers Team",
                     "page": "General History",
                     "date_time": {
                        "type": "gregory",
                        "year": "2024",
                        "month": "06",
                        "day": "13"
                     }
                  }
               ],
               "date_time": null,
               "isTable": false,
               "imgdesc": "",
               "format": "html",
               "PostMention": ""
            }
         ]
      },
      {
         "id": "SECTION_filling",
         "text": [
            {
               "text": "### Filling the *Yupana*\n\n",
               "source": null,
               "date_time": null,
               "isTable": false,
               "imgdesc": "",
               "format": "markdown",
               "PostMention": ""
            },
            {
               "text": "<p class=\"desc\"><img id=\"imgTawantsuyu\" onclick=\"htImageZoom('imgTawantsuyu', '0%')\" src=\"\" class=\"imgcenter\"/><b>Figure 1</b>: Map of South America highlighting the region from Colombia to Argentina and Chile, representing the areas once occupied by the ancient Inca Empire (<i>Tawantinsuyu</i>) (<htcite0>). The delimited area is shown approximately to provide the reader with a clearer understanding. © Mapswire (<i><htcite1></i>).</p>",
               "source": [
                  {
                     "type": 1,
                     "uuid": "ed31f80e-ddd3-448a-9331-a0b6ac5f82fd",
                     "text": "Hechler, R. S.",
                     "page": "",
                     "date_time": {
                        "type": "gregory",
                        "year": "2022",
                        "month": "10",
                        "day": "27"
                     }
                  },
                  {
                     "type": 1,
                     "uuid": "10cd855b-c2dc-4045-8a6c-f8486ef67cfa",
                     "text": "Mapswire",
                     "page": "",
                     "date_time": {
                        "type": "gregory",
                        "year": "-1",
                        "month": "-1",
                        "day": "-1"
                     }
                  }
               ],
               "date_time": [
                  {
                     "type": "gregory",
                     "year": "2022",
                     "month": "-1",
                     "day": "-1"
                  }
               ],
               "isTable": false,
               "imgdesc": "",
               "format": "html",
               "PostMention": ""
            },
            {
               "text": "Dhavit Prem studied the Yupana in the work of Felipe Guaman Poma de Ayala (<htcite0>), shown in Book 1 below. He concluded that, using repeated addition, the people of *Tawantinsuyu* (the territory of the Inca Empire) could also do *miray*, which means multiplication (<htcite1>).",
               "source": [
                  {
                     "type": 0,
                     "uuid": "f5b74f18-0bc4-46d2-8a5c-64dd80b74dd1",
                     "text": "Poma de Ayala, Felipe Guaman",
                     "page": "",
                     "date_time": {
                        "type": "gregory",
                        "year": "1615",
                        "month": "-1",
                        "day": "-1"
                     }
                  },
                  {
                     "type": 1,
                     "uuid": "a62b520a-f443-4d83-ab51-b99c9a46dab8",
                     "text": "Dhavit Prem",
                     "page": "pp. 360 - 361",
                     "date_time": {
                        "type": "gregory",
                        "year": "2018",
                        "month": "-1",
                        "day": "-1"
                     }
                  },
                  {
                     "type": 1,
                     "uuid": "2d2ea4a5-506b-4dbf-aaa4-3a10a8fbbd9c",
                     "text": "Dhavit Prem, Research Gate",
                     "page": "",
                     "date_time": {
                        "type": "gregory",
                        "year": "2018",
                        "month": "",
                        "day": ""
                     }
                  }
               ],
               "date_time": null,
               "isTable": false,
               "imgdesc": "",
               "format": "markdown",
               "PostMention": ""
            },
            {
               "text": "<p style=\"margin: auto; width: 100%;\"><iframe src=\"https://archive.org/details/primer-nueva-coronica-y-buen-gobierno-manuscrito/page/n361/mode/2up\" width=\"100%\" height=\"560\" frameborder=\"0\" webkitallowfullscreen=\"true\" mozallowfullscreen=\"true\" allowfullscreen></iframe></p><p class=\"desc\"><b>Book 1</b>: Page 362, Felipe Guaman Poma de Ayala's book.</p>",
               "source": null,
               "date_time": [
                  {
                     "type": "gregory",
                     "year": "2015",
                     "month": "4",
                     "day": "26"
                  }
               ],
               "isTable": false,
               "imgdesc": "On this image, we see an Indigenous man holding a quipu (knotted cords), with a numerical value indicated on the right. To the left, there is a Yupana—a board with dots representing numbers, possibly associated with finger counting.",
               "format": "html",
               "PostMention": ""
            },
            {
               "text": "According to the *Yupana Inka Tawa Pukllay* method by Dhavit Prem, the people of *Tawantinsuyu* first repeated the same number many times on the *Yupana*. Then they used the steps that Prem explained in his article. These steps are also in the text *Addition with the Yupana*",
               "source": [
                  {
                     "type": 1,
                     "uuid": "a62b520a-f443-4d83-ab51-b99c9a46dab8",
                     "text": "Dhavit Prem",
                     "page": "pp. 360 - 361",
                     "date_time": {
                        "type": "gregory",
                        "year": "2018",
                        "month": "-1",
                        "day": "-1"
                     }
                  },
                  {
                     "type": 1,
                     "uuid": "2d2ea4a5-506b-4dbf-aaa4-3a10a8fbbd9c",
                     "text": "Dhavit Prem, Research Gate",
                     "page": "",
                     "date_time": {
                        "type": "gregory",
                        "year": "2018",
                        "month": "",
                        "day": ""
                     }
                  },
                  {
                     "type": 1,
                     "uuid": "1bb0274d-dc51-4740-ac62-4d157b06ad88",
                     "text": "History Tracers Team",
                     "page": "Yupana (Addition)",
                     "date_time": {
                        "type": "gregory",
                        "year": "2024",
                        "month": "-1",
                        "day": "-1"
                     }
                  }
               ],
               "date_time": null,
               "isTable": false,
               "imgdesc": "",
               "format": "markdown",
               "PostMention": "."
            }
         ]
      },
      {
         "id": "SECTION_yupana",
         "text": [
            {
               "text": "### Multiplying with the *Yupana*\n\nTo understand the *Yupana Inka Tawa Pukllay* method better, we will use a Yupana with 4 rows. We will multiply one number by another using repeated addition. With this setup, we can show values up to **9,999**. But we can add more rows to multiply bigger numbers. There is no limit.\n\n#### The Yupana in this section\n\nAs soon as the page loads, the Yupana starts with the first level and with a multiplication to do.\n\nBetween the bar with the buttons \"🎲 New Exercise\" and \"⭐ Next Level\" and the button \"➡️ Next Step\", you will see an instruction. It shows the movements to do at the current stage. When you finish the stage correctly, a message will appear at the bottom of the Yupana to congratulate you.\n\nFollow the steps until you finish the calculation. First, put the number to multiply on the Yupana. Then, add it as many times as the multiplier says. To enter a number, click on any cell of the row on the Yupana. Each click changes the digit of that row from 0 to 9, over and over.\n\nYou can do as many exercises as you want at the same level. To do that, just click \"🎲 New Exercise\" after you finish a calculation.\n\nIf you already feel good about the current level, you can learn more by going to the next level. Use the \"⭐ Next Level\" button.",
               "source": null,
               "date_time": null,
               "isTable": false,
               "imgdesc": "",
               "format": "markdown",
               "PostMention": "."
            },
            {
               "text": "<style>.yupana-panel { background: #2e241f; border-radius: 50px; padding: 8px 18px; margin-bottom: 15px; margin-top: 15px; box-shadow: inset 0 2px 3px rgba(0,0,0,0.4), 0 3px 6px rgba(255,245,190,0.3); } .yupana-panel .exercise-header { display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: center; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 8px; } .level-badge { background: #ffb347; color: #1f2a0e; font-weight: bold; padding: 4px 14px; border-radius: 30px; font-size: clamp(0.8rem, 3vw, 1rem); white-space: nowrap; } .problem-display { background: #f2ecd8; padding: 4px 16px; border-radius: 35px; font-family: 'Courier New', monospace; font-weight: bold; font-size: clamp(1rem, 4vw, 1.5rem); color: #1f2a0e; white-space: nowrap; } .ex-btn { background: #846b4e; border: none; color: #ffefcf; font-weight: bold; font-size: clamp(0.7rem, 2.5vw, 0.9rem); font-family: inherit; padding: 6px 14px; border-radius: 50px; cursor: pointer; transition: 0.2s; } .ex-btn:hover { background: #a58a6a; transform: scale(1.03); } .ex-btn.hidden { display: none; } .step-panel { padding: 8px 0; color: #ffefcf; font-size: clamp(0.8rem, 2.5vw, 1rem); } .step-status { font-size: clamp(0.7rem, 2vw, 0.85rem); opacity: 0.9; margin-top: 4px; color: #ffefcf; } .feedback-area { text-align: center; margin: 10px 0; font-size: clamp(0.9rem, 3vw, 1.2rem); } .congrats { color: #2e7d32; font-weight: bold; } .success-message { color: #1565c0; } .mult-table { color: #ffefcf; font-family: 'Courier New', monospace; font-weight: bold; font-size: clamp(0.8rem, 2.5vw, 1rem); text-align: center; margin: 6px 0; } .mult-table .mult-row { padding: 2px 0; } .mult-table .mult-row strong { color: #ffb347; } .next-step-btn { display: block; margin: 10px auto; background: #2e7d32; border: none; color: white; font-weight: bold; font-size: clamp(0.9rem, 3vw, 1.1rem); font-family: inherit; padding: 10px 30px; border-radius: 50px; cursor: pointer; transition: 0.2s; } .next-step-btn:hover { background: #388e3c; transform: scale(1.03); } .next-step-btn.hidden { display: none; } #yupana1 { zoom: 0.7; }</style>",
               "source": null,
               "date_time": null,
               "isTable": false,
               "imgdesc": "",
               "format": "html",
               "PostMention": ""
            },
            {
               "text": "<p><table id=\"yupana1\" class=\"tawapukllay\"><tr><th colspan=\"4\"><i>Yupana</i></th></tr> <tr id=\"tf1\"><td id=\"tc1f1\"><span class=\"dot five_dot_c1_up\"></span><span class=\"dot five_dot_c1_center\"></span><span class=\"dot five_dot_c1_bottom\"></span><span class=\"dot five_dot_c2_up\"></span><span class=\"dot five_dot_c2_bottom\"></span></td> <td id=\"tc2f1\"><span class=\"dot three_dot_bottom\"></span><span class=\"dot three_dot_up\"></span><span class=\"dot three_dot_center\"></span></td> <td id=\"tc3f1\"><span class=\"dot two_dot_bottom\"></span> <span class=\"dot two_dot_up\"></span></td> <td id=\"tc4f1\"><span class=\"dot dot_center\"></span></td></tr> <tr id=\"tf2\"><td id=\"tc1f2\"><span class=\"dot five_dot_c1_up\"></span><span class=\"dot five_dot_c1_center\"></span><span class=\"dot five_dot_c1_bottom\"></span><span class=\"dot five_dot_c2_up\"></span><span class=\"dot five_dot_c2_bottom\"></span></td> <td id=\"tc2f2\"><span class=\"dot three_dot_bottom\"></span><span class=\"dot three_dot_up\"></span><span class=\"dot three_dot_center\"></span></td> <td id=\"tc3f2\"><span class=\"dot two_dot_bottom\"></span> <span class=\"dot two_dot_up\"></span></td> <td id=\"tc4f2\"><span class=\"dot dot_center\"></span></td></tr> <tr id=\"tf3\"><td id=\"tc1f3\"><span class=\"dot five_dot_c1_up\"></span><span class=\"dot five_dot_c1_center\"></span><span class=\"dot five_dot_c1_bottom\"></span><span class=\"dot five_dot_c2_up\"></span><span class=\"dot five_dot_c2_bottom\"></span></td> <td id=\"tc2f3\"><span class=\"dot three_dot_bottom\"></span><span class=\"dot three_dot_up\"></span><span class=\"dot three_dot_center\"></span></td> <td id=\"tc3f3\"><span class=\"dot two_dot_bottom\"></span> <span class=\"dot two_dot_up\"></span></td> <td id=\"tc4f3\"><span class=\"dot dot_center\"></span></td></tr> <tr id=\"tf4\"><td id=\"tc1f4\"><span class=\"dot five_dot_c1_up\"></span><span class=\"dot five_dot_c1_center\"></span><span class=\"dot five_dot_c1_bottom\"></span><span class=\"dot five_dot_c2_up\"></span><span class=\"dot five_dot_c2_bottom\"></span></td> <td id=\"tc2f4\"><span class=\"dot three_dot_bottom\"></span><span class=\"dot three_dot_up\"></span><span class=\"dot three_dot_center\"></span></td> <td id=\"tc3f4\"><span class=\"dot two_dot_bottom\"></span> <span class=\"dot two_dot_up\"></span></td> <td id=\"tc4f4\"><span class=\"dot dot_center\"></span></td></tr></table></p>",
               "source": null,
               "date_time": null,
               "isTable": false,
               "imgdesc": "The Yupana consists of a table with four columns and five rows: The first column contains five circles; The second column has three circles; The third column has two circles; The last column contains only one circle; This pattern repeats across all rows.",
               "format": "html",
               "PostMention": ""
            },
            {
               "text": "<p class=\"desc\"><b>Table 1</b>: Representation of the Yupana according to Poma de Ayala (<htcite0> ; <htcite1>).</p>",
               "source": [
                  {
                     "type": 1,
                     "uuid": "a62b520a-f443-4d83-ab51-b99c9a46dab8",
                     "text": "Prem, Dhavit",
                     "page": "pp. 355,",
                     "date_time": {
                        "type": "gregory",
                        "year": "2018",
                        "month": "04",
                        "day": "01"
                     }
                  },
                  {
                     "type": 0,
                     "uuid": "f5b74f18-0bc4-46d2-8a5c-64dd80b74dd1",
                     "text": "Poma de Ayala, Felipe Guaman",
                     "page": "pp. 361 - 362,",
                     "date_time": {
                        "type": "gregory",
                        "year": "1615",
                        "month": "02",
                        "day": "13"
                     }
                  }
               ],
               "date_time": [
                  {
                     "type": "gregory",
                     "year": "2018",
                     "month": "-1",
                     "day": "-1"
                  },
                  {
                     "type": "gregory",
                     "year": "1615",
                     "month": "-1",
                     "day": "-1"
                  }
               ],
               "isTable": false,
               "imgdesc": "",
               "format": "html",
               "PostMention": ""
            },
            {
               "text": "<div class=\"yupana-panel\"><div class=\"exercise-header\"><span class=\"level-badge\" id=\"levelBadge\">✖ Multiply by 1</span><span class=\"problem-display\" id=\"problemDisplay\">7 × 8</span><button class=\"ex-btn\" id=\"resetTutorBtn\">🎲 New Exercise</button><button class=\"ex-btn\" id=\"nextLevelBtn\">⭐ Next Level</button></div><button class=\"ex-btn\" id=\"resetButton\">↺ Reset</button><div class=\"step-panel\" id=\"stepMessage\">🧮 Click 'New exercise' to start</div><div class=\"step-status\" id=\"stepStatus\"></div><div class=\"feedback-area\" id=\"feedbackArea\"></div><div class=\"mult-table\" id=\"multTable\"></div><button class=\"next-step-btn\" id=\"nextStepBtn\">➡️ Next Step</button></div><div class=\"text-store\" style=\"display:none;\"><span id=\"txt_level\">✖ Multiply by</span><span id=\"txt_stepPrefix\">🧮</span><span id=\"txt_correctMessage\">✅ Correct! Click 'Next step' to continue.</span><span id=\"txt_movementISKAY\">ISKAY</span><span id=\"txt_movementKIMSA\">KIMSA</span><span id=\"txt_movementPISQA\">PISQA</span><span id=\"txt_movementPICHANA\">PICHANA</span><span id=\"txt_movementKINKIN\">KINKIN</span><span id=\"txt_movementsMessage\">✅ Correct! Movement(s) performed in {placeName}: <strong>{movements}</strong>. Click 'Next step' to continue.</span><span id=\"txt_noMovementsMessage\">✅ Correct! No movement needed in {placeName}. Click 'Next step' to continue.</span><span id=\"txt_carryConfirmMessage\">✅ Correct! The carried <strong>1</strong> was placed in {nextPlace}, shown in <strong>red on the opposite side</strong> (<strong>{movements}</strong>). Click 'Next step' to continue.</span><span id=\"txt_carrying\">carrying</span><span id=\"txt_perfectMessage\">🎉🎉🎉 PERFECT! 🎉🎉🎉<br>{value} × {times} = {result}<br>Great job using the Yupana!</span><span id=\"txt_congratsMessage\">🎉🎉🎉 CONGRATULATIONS! 🎉🎉🎉<br>You calculated {value} × {times} = {result}<br>Click 'New exercise' to practice more!</span><span id=\"txt_finalLevelMessage\">🎉🏆 ALL LEVELS COMPLETE! 🏆🎉<br>You mastered multiplication on the Yupana! Click 'New exercise' to start again at level 1.</span><span id=\"txt_lastLevelMessage\">🏅 Congratulations! You reached the last level! 🏅</span><span id=\"txt_step1Instruction\">📌 <strong>Step 1:</strong> Set the first value <strong>{value}</strong> by clicking on the Yupana squares.</span><span id=\"txt_step2Instruction\">📌 <strong>Step 2:</strong> Add the value <strong>{value}</strong> by clicking on the Yupana squares.</span><span id=\"txt_step1DigitInstruction\">📌 <strong>Step {step}:</strong> Set the <strong>{digit}</strong> in the {placeName} by clicking on the Yupana squares of that row.</span><span id=\"txt_step2DigitInstruction\">📌 <strong>Step {step}:</strong> Add the <strong>{digit}</strong> in the {placeName} by clicking on the Yupana squares of that row.</span><span id=\"txt_evalSimple\">➕ <strong>Step {step}:</strong> {digitA} + {digitB} = <strong>{result}</strong>. Place <strong>{result}</strong> in the {placeName} by clicking on the Yupana squares.</span><span id=\"txt_evalCarryDigit\">⚡ <strong>Step {step}:</strong> {digitA} + {digitB} = <strong>{total}</strong>. Place <strong>{resultDigit}</strong> in the {placeName}.</span><span id=\"txt_evalZero\">⚡ <strong>Step {step}:</strong> {placeName} will be {total}: {digitA} + {digitB} = <strong>{total}</strong>. Since the result in the row is <strong>0</strong>, you don't need to place anything on the Yupana.</span><span id=\"txt_carryFinalInstruction\">➕ <strong>Step {step}:</strong> Add the carried <strong>1</strong> to the next column by clicking on the Yupana squares. It will appear in <strong>red on the opposite side</strong>.</span><span id=\"txt_finalInstruction\">🎉 <strong>Verify:</strong> {value} × {times} = <strong>{result}</strong>. The markers on the Yupana should match this result.</span><span id=\"txt_stepStatus\">📖 Step {current}/{total}</span><span id=\"txt_welcomeMessage\">Click 'New exercise' to start. Click on the Yupana rows to arrange the value.</span><span id=\"txt_units\">Units</span><span id=\"txt_tens\">Tens</span><span id=\"txt_hundreds\">Hundreds</span><span id=\"txt_thousands\">Thousands</span><span id=\"txt_next\">next</span></div>",
               "source": null,
               "date_time": null,
               "isTable": false,
               "imgdesc": "",
               "format": "html",
               "PostMention": ""
            },
            {
               "text": "We also suggest watching the videos on the *Yupana Inka* channel. This way you can learn more about the work of Dhavit Prem and the Yupana Inka Association",
